1:# Semantic pass contracts
5:## Definition APIs
24:## Writing a contract
61:- `requires` runs before the kernel. Failed requirements prevent execution.
62:- `ensures` checks output properties or relational invariants before acceptance.
63:- `establishes` checks and records a newly established output fact.
64:- `preserves` checks that an input property holds and remains valid for an output. `mode:'check'` runs the target checker; `mode:'transfer'` requires a declared correspondence and an executable authorized transfer rule.
65:- `correspondence` requires supplied records naming exact input/output artifact revisions and the declared relation.
66:- `effects` governs access through the revisioned resource port.
67:- `cache` is `pure`, `tracked` or `never`. Pure definitions declare no resource effects. Writes require `never`.
71:## Analysis manager API
108:## Evidence and transfer
112:- `declared`: an assertion was recorded, without verification; `ok` is false for authorization purposes.
113:- `checked`: the specified checker ran or its exact valid evidence was reused.
114:- `transferred`: an existing valid result was carried to another revision after an authorized transfer checker verified the explicit correspondence.
115:- `proof`: the property-specific external certificate verifier accepted a supplied certificate.
