1:# Strategy IR v1
5:## Public API
40:### Algorithm registry
48:### Values and lexical references
56:### Operators
80:## Failure, concurrency and budgets
92:## Validation, editing and interchange
94:- `validate(value, registry?)` returns `{valid, issues}` with paths and codes. It checks JSON shape, format version, exact fields, IDs, references, lexical binding availability, algorithm categories/versions and numeric bounds.
95:- `assertValid(value, registry?)` throws `PlanValidationError` with the same issues.
96:- `walk(plan, visitor?)` returns ordered `{node,parent?,path,depth,slot?}` visits and optionally calls `visitor(node, visit)` in preorder; `find(plan,id)` or `find(plan,predicate)` returns the first matching node or undefined (`predicate(node, visit)`); `childNodes(node)` exposes direct structural children.
97:- `replace(plan,id,node)`, `insertBefore(plan,id,node)`, `insertAfter(plan,id,node)` and `remove(plan,id)` return new immutable validated plans. Invalid operations leave the old plan untouched. Insertions create a fresh sequence when the target has no sequence parent. Removal supports list entries; a required child or root must be replaced explicitly (an empty sequence is identity).
98:- `diff(before,after)` reports added, removed, changed and moved nodes by stable node ID. Composite changes refer to child IDs rather than duplicating entire descendant trees. Plan metadata changes use the `$plan` pseudo-ID.
99:- `serialize(plan, pretty=true)` uses deterministic key ordering; `deserialize(text, registry?)` validates and freezes the JSON interchange value. The workbench has its own lossless YAML view/editor; persisted plan bytes remain normal data.
