## Root changes and alternatives

~~~mermaid
flowchart LR
    I[Input revisions and parameters] --> F[Query analysis facts]
    F --> E[Check eligibility]
    E --> C[Prepare candidate and draft]
    C --> V[Discharge policy obligations]
    V --> P[Publish accepted heads]
    E --> R[Record attempt and evidence]
    C --> R
    V --> R
    P --> R
~~~

A transformation and its receipt give the layers a common semantic boundary. IR projections define what can be inspected and edited. Graph and dependence providers compute facts. Policy defines admissible evidence. Strategy decides which transition to request next. Aim for a single interpretation of identity, rollback, and publication. Prefer the native fast path for building candidates whose edits can be independently checked. The split between core tasks and pass declarations, and the separate preparation paths for native and editable results, are the first boundaries to test. "'`src/framework/core/types.ts:80`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:193`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:302`.

| Alternative considered | Decision and discriminating test |
| --- | --- |
| Promote a common SSA or graph storage layout to the framework'"'s universal IR | Reject. Canonicalizing every native AST, schedule and RV32 representation prematurely makes representation costs mandatory. Preserve stable scoped projections and typed cross-IR relations. Compare full projections to region-local or lazy ones on a small native pass and a real corpus edit. "'`src/framework/ir/adapters.ts:235`, `src/typed/ir.ts:411`, `src/tensor/ir.ts:140`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:36`. |
| Keep separate synchronous and asynchronous strategy languages | Reject. A plan'"'s meaning and supported operators would depend on its evaluator. Run native callbacks through the existing interpreter for plan composition, and share the single transformation lifecycle for synchronous APIs. Revisit a single effect-polymorphic implementation only if a useful synchronous plan cannot be factored into local transitions. P2 gives a parity test. "'`src/framework/strategy/interpreter.ts:134`, `T6-E/src/framework/strategy/sync.ts:113`, `T6-H/src/framework/strategy/sync.ts:145`. |
| Use `PassSpec.legal` as the entire check, or fold legality into a comparison after execution | Reject both. The first leaves candidate construction unchecked. The second may run an ineligible GPU kernel or a transformation that assumed a particular input form. Carry a precondition witness into postvalidation and distinguish unknown eligibility from disagreement. `T6-D/src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:169`, `T6-D/tests/tensor/schedule.test.mjs:85`, `T6-D/tests/tensor/schedule.test.mjs:113`. |
| Use the same verifier callback for all assurance levels | Reject. Report scope and method as structured data. A sampled equality comparison, exhaustive check over a finite domain, and a witness verified by a semantic kernel establish distinct claims. Reuse differential testing for empirical regression detection and counterexamples. `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:283`, `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:377`, `src/framework/contracts/analysis-manager.ts:879`. |
| Replace the optimizer with equality saturation or full polyhedral scheduling | Defer as a bounded experiment. Both are good candidate generators in the regions their theories model. Run one pure arithmetic window or one static-control loop nest through a second generator and compare the certified fragment, search cost, and output quality. Keep imperative and target-specific passes available for effects, traps, ABI, GPU synchronization and resource constraints. `src/typed/analyses.ts:40`, `src/typed/rules/compile.ts:119`, `src/tensor/fusion.ts:83`, `src/tensor/cuda-source.ts:368`. |
| Merge all T6 operations into the old planner or mandate a second full compiler implementation for schedule validation | Reject both. Move legality facts and schedule operations apart. Start with a small independent checker over normalized access and event order witnesses. A fuller schedule evaluator can be valuable for diagnosis and interpreter/backend consistency, as the E cell demonstrates in source. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:142`, `T6-E/src/tensor/schedule-eval.ts:57`, `T6-E/src/tensor/schedule-eval.ts:399`. |

## Ordered migration and decision gates

Each stage has a bounded fixture and a deletion target. A gate measures behavior before the next abstraction is widened. When the old behavior knowingly admits a weaker output, retain the discrepancy as a counterexample and require the new result to satisfy the stated policy.

| Order | Small change | What it can delete | Check and measurement |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Make evidence scope explicit and fix exact-by-default classification. Add a narrow differential job protocol with separate case, observation and verdict keys. Start with a local Typed worker and injected CUDA batches. `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:55`, `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:377`, `src/typed/meaning-exec.ts:14`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:131`. | Default-to-exact and dummy per-case requirements for batch-only validators. | Warm/cold equality, bad reuse keys, failed batch retries, duplicate concurrent requests, host/profile changes, mutated cases, all-inconclusive results. Report observed runs, remote dispatches, cache hit rates and time to first verdict. |
| 2 | Introduce the transformation receipt and one acceptance path for Tix inline and Typed fold. Run checks before publication with private candidate projections. Make the existing interpreter call the common path. Model store publication and semantic/resource commits as ordered operations with shared rejection semantics. `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:201`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:225`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:347`, `src/framework/contracts/analysis-manager.ts:1577`, `src/framework/passes/bridge.ts:29`. | Tix'"'s application loop and external gate hookup once the normal entry point consumes receipts. Remove duplicate lifecycle code as existing users move. | P1/P2 parity. Add postvalidation and false preservation failures, cancellation, common no-op receipt, two sibling attempts from one input, and one successful compare-and-swap. Compare both corpus revisions and reasons, allocations, sync-call latency and JS build size. Keep pure synchronous execution if a source API or measured cost warrants it. |
| 3 | Use the same transformation path for Tix-to-CUDA and one Typed backend step. Register named entity scopes. Add "'`setRoot` with CFG shape checks as a small edit extension. `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:203`, `src/typed/backend/compile.ts:369`, `src/framework/ir/transactions.ts:293`. | Domain-specific correspondence conversions and B1 entry-array mutation once those callers migrate. | Compare returned artifact bytes, correspondence roots and exact intermediate universes. Inject a foreign entity reference, removed root, and failed second output. Check head atomicity and measure scoped projection costs. |
| 4 | Emit checked rule applications in Typed fold/simplify and occurrence lineage for Tix inline. Feed D1 and A0 from a shared receipt reader. `src/typed/rules/passes.ts:14`, `src/tensor/passes.ts:21`, `src/typed/attribute.ts:140`. | Replay-based classifier logic for migrated rules and string-based attribution joins where lineage is explicit. | Freeze the A0 denominator and report both edit groups and affected unique sites. Compare producer witnesses against retrospective categories with a confusion matrix. Seed wrong rule, substitution, guard and scope mutants. Track rule coverage, check time, unexplained delta and many-to-many coverage. |
| 5 | Extract one CFG provider (including multi-latch natural loops) and a small memoized specializer. Run Typed LICM, then B1 on an integer VM subset, then a second static buffer region. Keep refusal for unsupported effects. `src/typed/analyses.ts:215`, `B1-A/src/typed/specialize-memory.ts:54`, `B1-B/src/typed/residualize.ts:55`, `B1-G/src/typed/bta.ts:65`. | Local worklists, duplicate CFG skeleton, and direct entry mutation in the migrated instances. | P2 and an irreducible CFG, plus dynamic branch joins, budget exhaustion, repeated specialization, invalid encodings, OOB reads and traps. Measure state count, residual size, no-trap/trap agreement, specialized RV32 instructions and compile time. Compare online liveness-keyed exploration with an offline binding-time division on the same cases. |
| 6 | Expose Tix access-dependence facts for pointwise fusion, then ordered contraction on a single supported subset. Factor the current schedule seed, add one fusion or split candidate and lower solely from the resulting checked plan. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:83`, `src/tensor/fusion.ts:142`, `src/tensor/cuda-source.ts:639`, `T6-D/src/tensor/schedule.ts:539`. | Duplicated shape/index tests where the extracted analysis subsumes them, and redundant re-planning from the emitter. | Exact reference results and accepted partitions vs today on eligible cases. Reorder-dependence, tail, zero-size, alias, and overflow mutants. Compare a restricted symbolic checker to an independent enumerator over tiny legal domains. Measure analysis cost, refusals and missed valid fusions, correspondence fidelity, generated-source size and GB10 performance. |
| 7 | Run a constrained choice over two Tix variants and one Typed pipeline pair. Record the policy as data and compare as a stationarity-controlled experiment. Expand incremental locality only where traces show actual demand. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:135`, `src/tensor/cuda-runtime.ts:106`, `src/framework/strategy/builders.ts:54`, `src/typed/attribute.ts:185`. | Hard-coded handoffs between tuning rules and generated guards where the shared variant covers their semantics. | Forced alternatives and default selection on the same case, held-out shapes, paired and interleaved timing, no-regression tolerance declared before evaluation, compile count and profile provenance. Count framework and domain glue changes for both uses. Stop expanding if instance cost and observability fail to improve. |

For compile overhead, record wall time, peak retained revisions and bytes, scope sizes, cache misses, verified transfers, and number of projected entities. For semantics, publish the checked domain, method, and surviving positive and negative witnesses. For generated performance, distinguish deterministic RV32 instructions from device time and from static counts. Report the two domains independently before treating any shared mechanism as a net simplification.

## Open questions

1. What stable occurrence identity should Tix give a substituted expression? Test source-anchor plus expansion path against explicit allocated IDs. Both need matching across unchanged regions, and cloned occurrences need distinct identities. `src/tensor/passes.ts:16`, `src/tensor/ir.ts:102`.
2. Which part of a receipt may be reused across semantically equal but differently identified artifacts? Test lineage reattachment with an independent membership check and retain exact keys for evidence until a verified dependency slice is available. `src/framework/core/runtime.ts:753`, `src/framework/contracts/analysis-manager.ts:1087`.
3. What strict FP observation model is sustainable across different targets? Decide NaN class, signed zero, math library and fused operations, then test subnormals, cancellation, thresholds, and asymmetry of error bounds. `src/tensor/contract.ts:100`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:105`.
4. How much of each T6 schedule is an algorithmic witness and how much is placement choice? Start with relation preservation for one contraction. Expand verification only after the schedule semantics and emitter boundary can be checked independently. `T6-D/src/tensor/schedule.ts:339`, `T6-E/src/tensor/schedule-eval.ts:57`, `T6-J/src/tensor/schedule.ts:309`.
5. Which specialization refusal cases deserve support as effects versus static assumptions? Compare immutable buffers and frame promotion first. Preserve program-counter, failure, and memory effects at the residual boundary. `B1-A/src/typed/specialize-memory.ts:85`, `B1-B/src/typed/residualize.ts:18`, `B1-G/src/typed/specialize-buffer.ts:98`.
6. Can a projection avoid scanning unrelated regions while retaining useful generic diff and retention guarantees? Measure against warm native execution. IRWB-009 gives a locality experiment before a persistent-store redesign is justified. `src/framework/ir/adapters.ts:235`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:201`.
