   123	// A fused kernel in block mode has a gate: at launch the host runs it fused, or its statements one by one, by the
   124	// shapes (fusion.ts). The recipe's shapes are small, so the rule alone would show little of one side. For a
   125	// program with a gate, every sample is therefore a case on each side, and the program is run once with each side
   126	// forced. A program without a gate has one case per sample.
   127	type Gate = 'fused' | 'unfused';
   128	const sides: readonly Gate[] = ['fused', 'unfused'];
   129	type CudaSample = ReturnType<typeof cudaCases>[number] & { gate?: Gate };
